  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000122514,
      "SummaryText": "Ascend Performance Materials - Chocolate Bayou - Alvin, TX                                                          11/03/2025\n\n1.0 Accidental Release Prevention Policies and Emergency Response Policies\nAPM Chocolate Bayou has a long and proud history of maintaining our processes in a safe and responsible manner.  We use a combination of accidental release prevention programs and emergency response planning programs to protect our employees, the environment, and the community.  \nAscend's vision for process safety is described below:\nWe will keep process energy (the Tiger) under our control, by: \n     - Knowing the scenarios that cause harm (the Risks); \n     - Knowing the safeguards that are in place to prevent or mitigate the Harm; \n     - Ensuring that the identified safeguards are effective for the relevant scenarios.\nAscend's values are:\n- Better Every Day: We invest in our people and our processes to improve every day.\n- Customer focused: We exist for our customers; they drive our actions. Their success is our success.\n- One Ascend: All together, with a common set of goals and eye toward the future.\n- We Care: We operate safely with high integrity for our employees, our customers and our communiaties.\n- Agile: We think broadly and lead proactively in a constantly evolving organization and industry.\n\n2.0 Facility and Regulated Substances Handled\nMultiple EPA RMP Covered chemicals are included at the Ascend Performance Materials (APM) Chocolate Bayou plant, including propylene, ammonia, acrylonitrile, hydrogen cyanide, hydrogen fluorine, sulfur dioxide, and formaldehyde. The EPA RMP Program 3 is applicable for relevant APM Chocolate Bayou processes.   In the Chocolate Bayou plant, APM owns and operates 6 facilities including AN2/3, AN7, Formalin, NTA, DSIDA (currently decommissioned) and ECU. There are 4 process units owned by guest companies and managed by APM personnel. While Tivoli Midstream CB1 LLC (\"Tivoli\") is the operating company for the distribution area"
    },
    {
